EBS Interview Questions 



1. Difference Between EBS and Instance Store

	EBS						Instance Store

	Persistent				Temporary
	Network storage			Physically attached
	Can snapshot			Cannot snapshot
	Safer					Data lost on stop


2. EBS Volume States


	State					Meaning

	Creating					Volume creation
	Available					Ready to attach
	In-use						Attached to EC2
	Deleting					Removing


3. Snapshot Notes

	Feature					Description

	Incremental				Only changed blocks stored
	Stored in S3			Managed by AWS
	Cross-region copy		Supported
	Encryption				Supported


4. Resize EBS Volume

	Increase size:

		→ Volumes → Modify Volume

	Then inside Linux:

		Check filesystem:

			lsblk

	Grow partition:

			sudo growpart /dev/xvda 1

	Resize filesystem:

		sudo resize2fs /dev/xvda1



5. Detach EBS Volume

	Go to:

		→ Volumes → Actions → Detach

	IMPORTANT:

		Unmount before detach:

		sudo umount /data

6. Delete EBS

	Delete only after:

		Snapshot created
		Data backup confirmed

	Delete:

		→ Volumes → Delete



